meta {
  name: Model Catalog - List
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/model-catalog?workspace_id={{workspaceId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  workspace_id: {{workspaceId}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const entry = res.body.data?.model_catalog?.[0];
    if (entry && entry.id) {
      bru.setVar("modelCatalogId", entry.id);
      bru.setVar("modelCatalogSlug", entry.slug);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  The public model picker for an agent's `model_catalog_id` or an
  `ask_ai` workflow node's `model_catalog_slug` config — not
  workspace-scoped, same as `Nodes - List (Global Catalog)`.

  Only active, non-internal catalog entries are returned, ordered by
  `sort_order` then name. Which real backend(s) serve an entry is never
  exposed here — see `Services\Ai\ModelCatalogResolver`.

  `workspace_id` — optional; a workspace the caller belongs to. Each
  entry is then described from that member's seat: `is_available`,
  `unavailable_reason`, `connect_providers`, `own_key`, `is_allowed`,
  `is_default`, `credits_per_message`. Without it (or for a workspace
  the caller isn't in) the platform view is used.

  `id` is what `Agents - Update`'s `model_catalog_id` and
  `Model Settings - Update` expect; `slug` is what an `ask_ai` node and
  `Model Catalog - Try` expect. Stores the first entry's as
  `modelCatalogId` / `modelCatalogSlug`.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { model_catalog: [{ id, slug, display_name, brand, description, strengths, speed, cost_tier, capabilities, retires_at, replacement_slug, ... }] } }`.
}
